{
  "id": "https://m-lancini.github.io/frida-vocab/dictionary/coeducation",
  "type": "Concept",
  "prefLabel": {
    "en": "coeducation"
  },
  "definition": {
    "en": "An educational model that promotes a non-sexist approach to teaching and learning by recognising and valuing the contributions of women and men on an equal basis."
  },
  "scopeNote": {
    "en": [
      "Its primary aim is to foster the full development and empowerment of both girls and boys, free from gender stereotypes and discriminatory practices. Coeducation goes beyond the concept of mixed-sex schooling, as research has shown that gender inequalities continue to persist within such educational settings. It entails the integration of the values, experiences, knowledge, and contributions of women and men throughout the educational process, thereby challenging and dismantling traditional gender hierarchies. It seeks to prepare students for active participation in both the public and private spheres of life, assigning equal social and educational value to each. Furthermore, coeducational practices create learning environments in which historically marginalised or invisible perspectives, experiences, and forms of knowledge are acknowledged and incorporated into the curriculum. This approach adopts a holistic perspective, addressing not only the needs and development of students but also the broader educational community, including teachers, families, and institutional structures"
    ]
  },
  "notation": [
    "5.1"
  ],
  "broader": {
    "id": "https://m-lancini.github.io/frida-vocab/dictionary/section-5",
    "prefLabel": {
